<title>CYPRUS: Woolworth H1 pre-tax gains up 39.8pct.</title>
<headline>Woolworth H1 pre-tax gains up 39.8pct.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months until June 30</p>
<p>(In millions of Cyprus pounds)</p>
<p>				    96		  95</p>
<p>Turnover		     15.500    vs     9.254</p>
<p>Pre-tax profit		1.025    vs	 733</p>
<p>Profit after tax		722    vs	 610</p>
<p>Returns to shareholders     674    vs	 610</p>
<p>Earnings per share (cents)  2.4    vs	 3.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is F.W. Woolworth (Cyprus) Ltd, a department store chain with four outlets on the island. Results include profits from the sale of the share capital of Zako Insurance Ltd, a subsidiary of affiliate company Zako Ltd.</p>
<p>Results also include a percentage of profits made by affiliate company Cyprus Trading Corporation from the sale of Afxo Insurance Ltd and Lemeco Industries Ltd earlier this year.</p>
<p>-- Nicosia newsroom 357 2 365089</p>
</text>
